From: TB351FU <dev@tb351fu>
Date: Thu Jul 9 00:00:00 2026
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Skip duplicate permission check for android package

framework-res.apk contains feature-flag-gated duplicate permission
declarations (e.g., SET_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT_FOR_CONTACTS) that are
intentional -- the runtime evaluates the aconfig flag to activate the
correct variant. The binary patcher that strips these attributes
breaks APK v2/v3 signing, so we fix this at runtime instead.

Upstream added EventLog logging (b/213323615) but still returns true
unconditionally.  We guard the return with a package-name check so
the android package's feature-flagged duplicates are allowed.

---
 .../pm/pkg/component/ParsedPermissionUtils.java    | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/pm/pkg/component/ParsedPermissionUtils.java b/frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/pm/pkg/component/ParsedPermissionUtils.java
index 0000000..0000000
--- a/frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/pm/pkg/component/ParsedPermissionUtils.java
+++ b/frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/pm/pkg/component/ParsedPermissionUtils.java
@@ -367,8 +367,12 @@ public class ParsedPermissionUtils {
                 final ParsedPermission perm = checkDuplicatePerm.get(name);
                 if (isMalformedDuplicate(parsedPermission, perm)) {
-                    // Fix for b/213323615
-                    EventLog.writeEvent(0x534e4554, "213323615");
-                    return true;
+                    // b/213323615 — featureFlag-gated duplicates are intentional in
+                    // the platform package and should not prevent the APK from loading.
+                    // The runtime will evaluate the feature flag to activate the correct variant.
+                    if (!"android".equals(pkg.getPackageName())) {
+                        EventLog.writeEvent(0x534e4554, "213323615");
+                        return true;
+                    }
                 }
                 checkDuplicatePerm.put(name, parsedPermission);
             }
